  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_knn_classifier(X_train: list, y_train: list, X_test: list, k: int = 3) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **KNN Classifier** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_knn_classifier(X_train: list, y_train: list, X_test: list, k: int = 3) -> list:\n    Xtr, ytr, Xte = np.array(X_train, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y_train, dtype=np.int64), np.array(X_test, dtype=np.float64)\n    return [int(np.bincount(ytr[np.argsort(np.linalg.norm(Xtr - x, axis=1))[:int(k)]]).argmax()) for x in Xte]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
